From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dimosus <dimosus.x@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:05:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] 10039: x86win.cspec: call fixup for the MSVC _ftol helpers

x86win.cspec: add a call fixup for the MSVC
 _ftol/_ftol2/_ftol2_sse helpers

The helpers take their argument in ST0, pop the x87 stack and return the
truncated value in EAX (EDX:EAX for _ftol2); no prototype can describe that,
so every call lost the converted expression.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../x86/data/languages/x86win.cspec           | 26 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86win.cspec b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86win.cspec
index 19c6a28786..89418108f7 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86win.cspec
+++ b/Ghidra/Processors/x86/data/languages/x86win.cspec
@@ -395,4 +395,30 @@
       ]]></body>
     </pcode>
 </callfixup>
+
+<callfixup name="ftol">
+  <target name="_ftol"/>
+  <target name="__ftol"/>
+  <target name="_ftol2"/>
+  <target name="__ftol2"/>
+  <target name="_ftol2_sse"/>
+  <target name="__ftol2_sse"/>
+  <target name="_ftol2_sse_excpt"/>
+  <target name="__ftol2_sse_excpt"/>
+  <pcode>
+   <body><![CDATA[
+    ftoltmp:8 = trunc(ST0);
+    EAX = ftoltmp:4;
+    EDX = ftoltmp(4);
+    ST0 = ST1;
+    ST1 = ST2;
+    ST2 = ST3;
+    ST3 = ST4;
+    ST4 = ST5;
+    ST5 = ST6;
+    ST6 = ST7;
+    ESP = ESP + 4;
+   ]]></body>
+  </pcode>
+</callfixup>
 </compiler_spec>
-- 
